  "headline": "Prabowo Proposes Sugiono and Amran as MPR Postpones VP Election",
  "seoTitle": "Sugiono and Amran Nominated as MPR Postpones VP Vote",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo nominated Sugiono and Amran for Vice President as the MPR confirmed the plenary session to select the successor has been moved to Dec 11.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto officially submitted Sugiono and Amran as candidates for the vacant Vice President position to the MPR.",
    "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) rescheduled the plenary session for the election and inauguration of the new Vice President to December 11, 2026.",
    "MPR leadership stated the delay is necessary to ensure adherence to established regulations and to address ongoing internal debates regarding selection rules."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia is currently managing the process to fill the vacant Vice President position following the departure of Gibran. MPR Speaker Ahmad Muzani announced that the plenary session originally intended for the selection and subsequent inauguration has been officially rescheduled for December 11, 2026. This decision follows deliberations within the assembly, with officials citing the need to ensure procedural consistency and compliance with regulatory requirements. In a significant development, President Prabowo Subianto has formally proposed Sugiono and Amran as candidates for the role. The assembly had previously established specialized working groups to verify credentials and oversee the selection process. MPR leadership recently met with the presidential palace to communicate the schedule change and coordinate the next steps for the constitutional vacancy.",
